1
00:00:00,728 --> 00:00:02,438
(Sheldon:)but it works for Princeton, too.

2
00:00:03,898 --> 00:00:05,898
(Amy:)Scavenger hunts at Harvard
were really tough.

3
00:00:06,067 --> 00:00:07,907
(Amy:)I always got stuck
on the first challenge.

4
00:00:08,069 --> 00:00:09,979
Trying to End someone
to be on a team with me.

5
00:00:12,073 --> 00:00:14,813
(Amy:)I guess that story's
more sad than funny.

6
00:00:17,211 --> 00:00:19,621
(Penny:)I love scavenger hunts. My friends
and I had them all the time.

7
00:00:19,781 --> 00:00:20,821
(Leonard:)Oh, these are a little different.

8
00:00:20,982 --> 00:00:23,122
(Leonard:)There's a tradition
at elite universities.

9
00:00:23,284 --> 00:00:24,664
(Howard:)And Princeton.

10
00:00:25,987 --> 00:00:29,627
(Leonard:)A tradition of hunts full of puzzles
that rely on logic,

11
00:00:29,791 --> 00:00:31,501
(Leonard:)obscure knowledge, science.

12
00:00:31,659 --> 00:00:34,159
(Penny:)Oh, in ours we would just run
around town looking for a store

13
00:00:34,329 --> 00:00:36,279
(Penny:)that would sell us beer.

14
00:00:37,665 --> 00:00:40,165
-So, who's in?
-I think it sounds fun.

15
00:00:40,335 --> 00:00:41,335
(Amy:)-Yeah, me, too.
-I'm in.

16
00:00:41,502 --> 00:00:43,502
(Various:)-Let's do it.
-I'm sorry.

17
00:00:43,671 --> 00:00:46,311
(Sheldon:)Are we really doing this
or are we tricking Koothrappali again

18
00:00:46,474 --> 00:00:48,114
(Sheldon:)like with the dinner party?

